---
description: Use Snipara as the project memory and source-backed context layer for Cursor agents.
alwaysApply: true
---

snipara-memory:

- When the user asks about prior project decisions, preferences, workflows, or reusable context, use the Snipara MCP tools before guessing from chat memory.
- Prefer the simple Snipara discovery path first: call `snipara_help` for tool guidance when the exact tool is unclear.
- Use source-backed context for repository questions when available; cite the files or memories returned by Snipara in the answer.
- At the end of substantial work, persist durable outcomes through Snipara only when they are reusable: decisions, workflows, architectural rationale, validated troubleshooting, or stable user preferences.
- Never store secrets, tokens, private keys, raw credentials, or one-off transient command noise in Snipara memory.
